OpenL2D's code is not included in this repository. The notebook downloads it
from the source above, at the commit above, and applies the four patch files
in patches/. Each patch file begins with a statement that this project
changed the OpenL2D files it names. The changes and their reasons:

  0001-expert_gen-w_dict-protected-weights.patch
    Changes: Code/synthetic_experts/expert_gen.py
    Why: it fixes a defect in OpenL2D. With the benchmark's own expert
    settings, one line builds the protected-attribute weights as a list
    of empty values, and a later line indexes into each of those empty
    values, so the expert generator stops with a type error before
    fitting any expert. This patch changes that one line.

  0002-dataset_cfg-protected-entry-customer_age.patch
    Changes: Code/alert_data/dataset_cfg.yaml
    Why: it fixes a defect in OpenL2D. The protected-attribute entry
    names the feature "age" with type "numeric". The generator's code
    tests for "numerical" or "categorical", and the dataset's column is
    "customer_age". So the attribute is silently not split at age 50,
    contrary to the code's own comment. This patch names "customer_age"
    with type "numerical".

  0006-testbed-drawn-teams-membership.patch
    Changes: Code/testbed/testbed_train_alert_generation.py and
    Code/testbed/cfg.yaml
    Why: adapted for this study (how the router's training teams are
    built).

  0009-testbed_cfg-destination_path_train-drawn-teams-relative.patch
    Changes: Code/testbed/cfg.yaml
    Why: adapted for this study (where the training files are written).

